Here's how you can round a single column to the nearest integer using the default rounding method:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable("myTable");
// Load data from a CSV file
await table.loadData("./data.csv");
// Round 'column1' to the nearest integer (default decimals=0, method='round')
await table.round("column1");
// Log the first rows to see the rounded values
await table.logTable();
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

Set the 'cache' option to true in the options object. Here's an example:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable("foodTable");
// Load sample data
await table.loadArray([
  { food: "pizza" },
  { food: "sushi" },
  { food: "burger" },
  { food: "pasta" },
  { food: "salad" },
  { food: "tacos" },
]);
// Generate embeddings for the 'food' column (assuming this step is done)
await table.aiEmbeddings("food", "embeddings", { cache: true });
// Find similar foods with caching the input text embedding
const similarFoods = await table.aiVectorSimilarity(
  "italian food",
  "embeddings",
  3,
  {
    cache: true, // Caches the embedding of the input text
  },
);
await similarFoods.logTable();
await sdb.done();
```

The `getNbColumns` method is asynchronous and returns a Promise that resolves to a number. Here's an example:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// Load some data
await table.loadData("./my-data.csv");
// Get the number of columns
const nbColumnsPromise = table.getNbColumns();

// Await the promise to get the number of columns
const nbColumns = await nbColumnsPromise;
console.log(nbColumns); // Output the number of columns
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

You can use the `unit` option to specify kilometers. Here's an example:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// We load geospatial data from a file
await table.loadGeoData("./my-geodata.geojson");
// Compute the length of line geometries in kilometers and store in 'length_km'
await table.length("length_km", { unit: "km" });
// We log the first rows
await table.logTable();
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

