If you don't specify the `decimals` option, the variance will be calculated without any rounding. Here's an example:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// We load data from a file
await table.loadData("./my-data.csv");
// We calculate the variance of the 'quantity' column without rounding
const quantityVariance = await table.getVar("quantity");
console.log(quantityVariance); // e.g., 25.523456789
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

The cache is invalidated if the `run` function's content changes or if the TTL expires. Here's an example:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// Cache the computations with TTL and function change invalidation
await table.cache(async () => {
  // Load data
  await table.loadData("items.csv");
  // Perform computations
  await table.summarize({
    values: "price",
    categories: "department",
    summaries: ["min", "max", "mean"]
  });
}, { ttl: 60 });
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

