```

If no geometry column is found, the method will throw an error. You should explicitly specify the column:
```
// We start a SimpleDB instance
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// Load data (no geometry column present)
await table.loadData("./data.csv");
// Attempting to compute centroid without specifying a column will fail
try {
  await table.centroid("centerPoint");
} catch (e) {
  console.error("Centroid computation failed: ", e.message);
}
// Specify the correct column to succeed
await table.centroid("centerPoint", { column: "geom" });
await table.logTable();
await sdb.done();
```

