The buffer distance is measured in the units of the geometry's Spatial Reference System (SRS). For example, if the geometries are in meters, the distance is in meters.

```ts
// We start a SimpleDB instance
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// Load geospatial data with SRS units in meters
await table.loadGeoData("./my-geodata.geojson");
// Create a buffer of 5 meters around geometries in the default column
await table.buffer("bufferedGeom", 5);
// Log the first rows
await table.logTable();
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

