Yes, you can use `updateWithJS` to convert a string column to a Date object. Here's an example:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable("myTable");
// We load data from the file
await table.loadData("./my-data.csv");
// We convert the 'dateColumn' string to a Date object
await table.updateWithJS((rows) => {
  const modifiedRows = rows.map((d) => ({
    ...d,
    dateColumn: typeof d.dateColumn === "string"
      ? new Date(d.dateColumn)
      : d.dateColumn,
  }));
  return modifiedRows;
});
// We log the first rows to see the updated data
await table.logTable();
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

