Here's how you can specify the geometry columns for the spatial join:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const tableA = sdb.newTable("tableA");
const tableB = sdb.newTable("tableB");
// Assuming both tables have been loaded with data
// We perform an intersection join, specifying geometry columns
await tableA.joinGeo(tableB, "intersect", {
  leftTableColumn: "geometryA",
  rightTableColumn: "geometryB",
});
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

