The `projection` option is required when adding a geometry column. It specifies the geospatial projection of the new geometry column. You can reuse the projection of an existing geometry column, which is available in `table.projections`. This ensures that the new geometry column is correctly aligned with other geospatial data in your table.
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// Assuming you have loaded geospatial data with a 'country' geometry column
// await table.loadGeoData("./my-geodata.geojson");
// Add a new geometry column 'centroid' using the centroid of the 'country' column
// The projection of the new 'centroid' column is set to be the same as 'country'.
await table.addColumn("centroid", "geometry", `ST_Centroid("country")`, {
  projection: table.projections.country,
});
// Log the first rows to see the new centroid column
await table.logTable();
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

