The `wider` method takes two arguments: `columnsFrom` and `valuesFrom`. Here's an example:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// We load data from a file
await table.loadData("./my-data.csv");
// We restructure the table by pivoting 'Year' into new columns with 'Employees' as values
await table.wider("Year", "Employees");
// We log the table to see the restructured data
await table.logTable();
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
