The `intersect` method requires both geometry columns to have the same projection. If they don't, it will throw an error. Here's how you can ensure they match before checking intersection:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// Start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// Create a table and load data
const table = sdb.newTable("geoTable");
await table.loadGeoData("./data1.geojson");
await table.loadGeoData("./data2.geojson");
// Reproject one column to match the other
await table.reproject("geomB", "EPSG:4326", "reprojectedGeomB");
// Now check intersection with matching projections
await table.intersect("geomA", "reprojectedGeomB", "intersects");
// Log and close
await table.logTable();
await sdb.done();
```

