await sdb.done();
```

Yes, you can use conditions to filter the top rows. Here's an example:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// Load your data first
await table.loadData("./yourdata.csv");
// Get top 3 rows where category is 'Technology'
const filteredTop = await table.getTop(3, { conditions: "category === 'Technology'" });
console.log(filteredTop);
// Close everything
await sdb.done();
```

